    "notes": "1. 'total_operating_cost' is constructed as the sum of Cost of sales, Marketing and selling expenses, General and administrative expenses, and Other operating income and expenses. This aligns with standard practice for a luxury goods company, capturing all major operational cost categories before operating profit. 2. 'Other operating income and expenses' is treated as a cost (positive value) as it is a net expense in all periods. 3. 'Interest on lease liabilities' is included in 'interest_expenses' as it is a recurring financial cost related to financing. 4. 'Other financial income and expenses' is excluded from 'interest_expenses' as it contains non-interest items like fair value adjustments and dividends. 5. 'Income/(Loss) from joint ventures and associates' is excluded from 'total_operating_cost' as it is a share of profit from equity investments, not an operating expense. 6. Values are extracted directly from the primary statement; parentheses indicate negative values in the source, which have been converted to positive numbers for cost/expense fields per the sign convention rule.",
